so it's very simple.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:20.710
Now then, let's go into, this is white, titanium white,

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.130
with the least little touch of the cad yellow.

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:25.650
Least little touch, can't say that enough times.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:29.200
All right, let's go back up here and let's begin.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.630
putting in some sparkle on this foam.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.060
The brush is sort of tilted to the side

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.840
and pushed upward so that bright area hits up here.

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:39.710
See it?

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:43.850
Begin running out of paint.

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.090
Turn the brush over, there's a whole other side.

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.670
And here it's crashing up.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.540
Oh, I ran out of paint.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.700
I got excited and ran out of paint.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.070
There we go, look at that.

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:57.550
It's splashing all up here against these rocks

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:58.350
and carrying on.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:16:59.980
Wipe your brush.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.940
clean it, try to keep that color as nice and pure as you can.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:13.800
In here, push it, make little sounds,

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:18.260
think about being at the ocean, look at that,

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.660
churning, flashing, it's a lot of power in here,

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.360
tremendous amount of power.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:29.980
Okay, let me, you wipe off the,

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.640
the excess paint, now come back in here with a brush

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:36.520
that's quite dry and has no paint, clean brush,

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.840
and just begin blending these areas together

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:43.400
using little circular strokes, little circular strokes,

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.970
tiny little circles, there you go, see there?

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:51.400
Now then, let me clean your brush.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.680
I must have cleaned 100,000 brushes and it's still fun.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.380
Now with a clean, dry brush,

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:07.010
I'm gonna go right in here, very gently.

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:09.970
We're just gonna mix this up, just stir it a little bit.

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:13.300
See there, look at that, brings all that together.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:18.860
Just don't let this get too bright.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.140
The only part you want to be really bright

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:22.950
is what's out in the sun.

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:27.060
Okay, now we need something for that to be crashing against.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.180
Tell you what, let's go right into some.

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:33.770
Van Dyke Brown here, pull it out very flat, like so.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:36.620
Cut across it so you have that roll of paint

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:38.160
right out on the edge of the knife.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:39.400
Let's go up here.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.380
Now this is crashing right in here,

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.850
so we need a big stone that lives, there it is.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:49.770
Look at that big old stone, he's living here.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.200
Waves are just about to beat him to death.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:59.770
There you go, this is nice.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.150
This is nice.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.320
This would be a good place to do some surf fishing.

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:09.620
You can catch a big ol' fish that lives out there in the ocean.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.140
My mother would like it.

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:13.650
She's quite a fisherman.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:17.410
She came to Alaska and spent some time with me,

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:19.790
took her out and she caught a big salmon.

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.830
Okay, this is a little dark sienna and Van Dyke brown.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.590
I want this to be quite dark still.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.420
And with this, we sort of form our rocks.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:35.110
See here, still quite dark, quite dark.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.840
Now, we'll take a fan brush,

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:41.370
and we'll go into a little liquid white,

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:47.120
a little titanium white, and then phthalo blue.

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.600
I want this to be a little thinner

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.440
than the paint that's already on the canvas.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.500
That's why I dipped it into the liquid white first.

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:56.480
Okay, now, let's go right up here.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:59.860
Now, with this color, you can just quickly here.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:05.720
put the indication of water just running right off this rock.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.990
Now if your paint doesn't want to stick,

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:11.960
you can add a little paint thinner,

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:13.440
a little more of the liquid white.

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:15.280
Look at there.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.190
And at home, when you have a lot of time,

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:21.260
you can sit and really put a lot of these in.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.740
I just want to show you how right now.

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:25.280
You can just go crazy.

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.640
All kinds of beautiful little things.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.780
Okay, go right in here.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:35.510
Again, laying in all kinds of little doers

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.820
right up to the rocks.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:41.800
Leave some of these dark areas showing,

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:44.850
make it look like little foam things happening.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.220
Don't just cover it all.

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:52.440
This is phthalo blue, titanium white,

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:55.570
and it's picking up that dark color that's already there.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.500
See, leave some of these dark areas

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:04.520
and worry about shape.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:08.430
Create all kinds of little shapes.

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:10.090
See, it's going right up the side there.

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:13.870
Leave little holes in it,

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:19.320
giving you the feeling of the ocean yet.

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:27.370
See, see how that makes it look like it's swirled?

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:29.970
Don't keep beating it though, hit it.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:31.010
and get away from it.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.430
Hit it, get away from it.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.950
There, kinds of little things.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.620
Now then, maybe in here we're gonna have some sand

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:44.960
and we want it to look wet.

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:50.970
So take a little white and I'm gonna just sort of pull this.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:55.240
Now we put color on the canvas already here.

00:21:56.780 --> 00:21:59.900
Now then, directly under here, pull straight.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:06.480
Put a little color right down like that,

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.570
and then lightly come across.

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:15.470
Add at least a little touch of dark sienna to that,

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:19.770
give it a little more dirt feeling.

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:26.700
Like, see there, down, and go across.

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:28.660
Just like we're making reflections on a lake.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.050
That easy, yeah.

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:36.240
Take the paint thinner, and go right into my blue color,

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:39.110
and maybe there's a little ripple that lives.

00:22:39.550 --> 00:22:41.950
Yep, right there, see?

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:43.620
Pull back some little lines.

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:44.900
These should be basically straight.

00:22:48.810 --> 00:22:51.410
Just make it look like water there.

00:22:51.590 --> 00:22:55.260
Go into a little bit of the lavender color,

00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:57.000
and right underneath this here,

00:22:57.320 --> 00:22:59.460
just make a little line, a little dark line.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.280
and that'll help make it look like

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:04.900
it's sort of standing up a little.

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:07.770
That little line is very important.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:19.150
Now, I still have that lavender color on my liner brush.

00:23:19.360 --> 00:23:21.760
I'll just put some little things in here.

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:24.570
Now, you can just put all kinds of little things

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:29.360
that are happening wherever you want them.

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:37.390
Okay, tell you what, there's a nice area over here.

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:38.570
Let's put another happy stone.

00:23:39.550 --> 00:23:42.370
Use the Van Dyke Brown again, pull it out very flat.

00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:44.490
That little roll of paint, and maybe this stone,

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:46.560
yep, he lives right there.

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:49.130
You knew that, didn't you?

00:23:51.140 --> 00:23:54.150
In your seascape, decide where you want stones to live.

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:58.240
Put them wherever you want them, wherever you want them.

00:23:58.280 --> 00:23:59.340
This is Van Dyke Brown.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.520
a little bit of the dark sienna in it.

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:03.590
Maybe it comes right on off the canvas there.

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:10.640
Just let these things happen.

00:24:12.010 --> 00:24:14.910
Then we'll take a little yellow ochre,

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.000
a little dark sienna, a little Van Dyke brown.

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:19.780
Mix them very loose.

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:23.000
Cut off a little roll of paint, okay?

00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:26.180
Now then, by loose I mean don't over mix them.

00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:29.810
See, that way you get all these beautiful things.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.290
They just, they happen, happen automatically.

00:24:33.530 --> 00:24:34.590
You don't have to worry about them.

00:24:35.940 --> 00:24:37.960
Shoot, spend your time that you're gonna think

00:24:37.990 --> 00:24:39.450
thinking about composition.

00:24:40.710 --> 00:24:42.470
It's nice when you don't have to think about

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:45.040
how to load that knife.

00:24:45.220 --> 00:24:47.000
You can spend all your thinking time

00:24:47.410 --> 00:24:49.630
just thinking about your composition.

00:24:51.510 --> 00:24:52.390
That's when you really,

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:55.200
you really experience the joy of painting.

00:24:56.760 --> 00:24:58.980
Add in a little bit of water right around those foots here.

00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:06.140
Now I'm gonna take a little more of that

00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:07.740
thalo blue and white,

00:25:09.320 --> 00:25:11.390
and let's have a little bit of water,

00:25:11.390 --> 00:25:13.130
maybe just dripping right off this rock.

00:25:14.190 --> 00:25:15.690
Here comes some, that.

00:25:16.610 --> 00:25:19.770
And you can really work on the shape of your rocks

00:25:19.770 --> 00:25:22.190
doing this, make all kinds of beautiful little things.

00:25:23.060 --> 00:25:25.220
It just goes on and on and on.

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:33.710
Now then, paint thinner, I wanna go back in here

00:25:33.710 --> 00:25:38.170
and I wanna begin adding just some little details.

00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:46.380
See, all these things really, really help you painting.

00:25:47.040 --> 00:25:48.940
All these little details, spend some time.

00:25:50.380 --> 00:25:51.700
You know, they yell and scream at me here

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:52.920
if I go over 30 minutes.

00:25:53.870 --> 00:25:56.740
But at home, you can do anything.

00:25:58.420 --> 00:25:58.780
Anything.

00:25:59.440 --> 00:25:59.800
Well, almost.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.520
I don't see anything, there.

00:26:06.330 --> 00:26:10.450
And now, kinds of little,

00:26:11.380 --> 00:26:18.660
these little details are what really make your seascape pretty.

00:26:19.710 --> 00:26:22.100
Little foamy patterns all over,

00:26:28.640 --> 00:26:29.880
little sandpiper or two.

00:26:30.060 --> 00:26:39.710
There, I think that'll show you how to do

00:26:39.710 --> 00:26:41.030
